{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>לץ היין</b> — [it is] deficient [i.e., the text lacks] 'a man'; 'wine is a scoffer' means it is הומה, i.e., crying out that they give it its wage." "<b>לא יחכם</b> — he will not learn wisdom while occupying himself with wine."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Resolved the ellipsis: Ibn Ezra notes the verse lacks the word 'man' before 'wine.' The phrase 'give it its wage' refers to wine demanding its recompense, i.e., intoxication."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:45.859782533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}